WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.710
Our recipe book is A4, which
is perfect for printing.

2
00:00:03.845 --> 00:00:08.095
But I'd like it on a reMarkable tablet
too, and that's a different shape.

3
00:00:08.244 --> 00:00:13.070
This episode is about variants:
one document, in several sizes.

4
00:00:13.278 --> 00:00:16.728
In Templates mode, the bar
at the top lists variants.

5
00:00:16.862 --> 00:00:19.262
There is one so far, called Default.

6
00:00:19.350 --> 00:00:23.099
A variant is a complete set of
templates for one page size.

7
00:00:23.165 --> 00:00:26.635
The pages and their fields
are shared by every variant.

8
00:00:26.840 --> 00:00:28.330
The plus adds one.

9
00:00:28.446 --> 00:00:32.450
I'll call it reMarkable, and choose
the Paper Pro from the size list.

10
00:00:32.567 --> 00:00:35.682
Auto-Reflow scales every
element to the new page,

11
00:00:35.682 --> 00:00:39.237
and Scale Typography shrinks
the text along with it.

12
00:00:39.442 --> 00:00:44.462
Create Variant copies every template,
fitted to the new size, and switches to it.

13
00:00:44.670 --> 00:00:47.406
Here's the recipe page
at the tablet's size.

14
00:00:47.519 --> 00:00:50.838
The reMarkable page is wider
for its height than A4,

15
00:00:50.838 --> 00:00:55.748
and reflow scales width and height
separately, so the whisk got squashed.

16
00:00:55.813 --> 00:00:58.933
I'll make it square again: 34 by 34.

17
00:00:59.819 --> 00:01:04.618
The A4 version is still there, untouched:
switching between them is just this

18
00:01:04.618 --> 00:01:05.429
dropdown.

19
00:01:05.572 --> 00:01:10.452
Each variant keeps its own templates, so
a fix in one never touches the other.

20
00:01:10.661 --> 00:01:15.681
Sizes are stored in points, and the unit
menu in Template Settings converts them.

21
00:01:15.799 --> 00:01:21.619
Switch to millimeters, and the
tablet page reads about 180 by 240.

22
00:01:21.825 --> 00:01:26.378
If you'll make more books like this one,
Save Preset turns the whole project into a

23
00:01:26.378 --> 00:01:27.451
starting point.

24
00:01:27.583 --> 00:01:30.013
Give it a name and a short description.

25
00:01:30.140 --> 00:01:34.860
Everything comes along: both variants,
every template, and the pages too.

26
00:01:35.943 --> 00:01:40.417
It now waits in the New Project
dialog, beside the built-in presets.

27
00:01:40.471 --> 00:01:43.921
Every project made from it
is an independent copy.

28
00:01:44.125 --> 00:01:47.703
Everything you have built
is one JSON document.

29
00:01:47.747 --> 00:01:52.691
The JSON button opens it, as a tree
you can browse, or as plain text.

30
00:01:52.729 --> 00:01:57.940
It is handy for bulk changes, and Apply
Changes lands any edit as a single undo

31
00:01:57.940 --> 00:01:58.519
step.

32
00:01:58.726 --> 00:02:01.896
Export PDF prints the
variant you are looking at.

33
00:02:01.989 --> 00:02:06.021
The All button beside it prints
every variant, one PDF each,

34
00:02:06.021 --> 00:02:07.884
named after its variant.

35
00:02:07.948 --> 00:02:12.166
And the greyscale button from episode
six works on all of them at once.

36
00:02:14.108 --> 00:02:18.067
Here's the reMarkable copy: the
same pages, with the same links,

37
00:02:18.067 --> 00:02:19.678
shaped for the tablet.

38
00:02:19.883 --> 00:02:24.353
Next time: the generator, where a few
lines of code build a whole planner.
